1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,986
CareSteps is a competition prototype for older adults managing an existing blood

2
00:00:05,006 --> 00:00:09,716
pressure care plan in Singapore. This is a fictional patient, Madam Tan.

3
00:00:10,006 --> 00:00:11,916
The app is not a medical service.

4
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:19,354
The home screen keeps the daily actions close: record a reading, check medicines, or

5
00:00:19,374 --> 00:00:25,224
explain what made self care difficult. The red help bar stays available across pages.

6
00:00:25,867 --> 00:00:27,996
I will record a blood pressure reading.

7
00:00:28,346 --> 00:00:32,656
Only the two numbers are required; the measurement time defaults to now.

8
00:00:33,246 --> 00:00:35,636
The page states that nothing has been saved yet.

9
00:00:37,633 --> 00:00:42,346
Here I enter one hundred forty five over eighty eight from the fictional home monitor.

10
00:00:42,776 --> 00:00:45,886
Optional fields can record a pulse or the patient's own words.

11
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:51,145
The first action prepares a draft and shows both numbers again.

12
00:00:51,515 --> 00:00:57,295
It has not written a reading. This explicit check helps catch a typing mistake before

13
00:00:57,315 --> 00:00:58,485
the record changes.

14
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:04,625
Now I confirm the draft. The reading appears in history with its measurement time.

15
00:01:05,875 --> 00:01:10,865
Earlier corrected rows remain visible, while statistics count only current readings.

16
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:16,634
My numbers shows a fourteen day window and the exact number of current readings used for

17
00:01:16,654 --> 00:01:21,524
each average. It does not classify any single measurement as safe or dangerous.

18
00:01:22,533 --> 00:01:27,348
The chart stops at gaps instead of drawing a reassuring line across missing days.

19
00:01:27,718 --> 00:01:32,228
A gap means there is no record; it cannot tell us whether a measurement was missed.

20
00:01:34,033 --> 00:01:38,426
I can expand the list to inspect each day, including those with no reading.

21
00:01:38,776 --> 00:01:43,246
The text table carries the same values as the chart for people who do not use graphics.

22
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:51,398
The distinctive feature begins here. Rather than calling a missing record noncompliance,

23
00:01:51,968 --> 00:01:58,068
CareSteps asks what was difficult. The person may describe it, select a category, or

24
00:01:58,088 --> 00:01:59,198
skip the question.

25
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:04,515
I write that the cuff is difficult to use and leave every category unselected.

26
00:02:04,985 --> 00:02:09,075
The next page explicitly says no reason has been given a name yet.

27
00:02:09,365 --> 00:02:11,635
The patient's words remain intact.

28
00:02:12,533 --> 00:02:17,008
Only after I choose a category does the app treat that reason as confirmed.

29
00:02:17,418 --> 00:02:22,398
A suggestion from a model would remain a suggestion until the person confirms or changes

30
00:02:22,418 --> 00:02:22,908
it.

31
00:02:23,400 --> 00:02:28,625
This page offers a different next step for a difficulty using equipment than it would

32
00:02:28,645 --> 00:02:31,175
for forgetting or running out of medicine.

33
00:02:31,565 --> 00:02:33,975
A support choice never changes a prescription.

34
00:02:34,600 --> 00:02:38,414
The medicine page lists the two fictional prescribed items.

35
00:02:38,744 --> 00:02:43,984
Each explanation is linked to a recorded source, and this prototype cannot decide a dose

36
00:02:44,004 --> 00:02:46,034
or change what a clinician prescribed.

37
00:02:47,567 --> 00:02:50,813
Notice the publisher, source link, and review status.

38
00:02:51,043 --> 00:02:54,973
These entries were checked by the team and have not received clinical review.

39
00:02:55,183 --> 00:02:57,973
That distinction appears where the explanation is displayed.

40
00:03:00,200 --> 00:03:03,057
The live assistant is available directly on the home page.

41
00:03:03,487 --> 00:03:09,647
I will ask one ordinary medicine question, then test a question it must refuse and a

42
00:03:09,667 --> 00:03:11,797
symptom that needs emergency routing.

43
00:03:12,433 --> 00:03:17,926
I ask what amlodipine is for. The app sends the question to its configured model and

44
00:03:17,946 --> 00:03:20,496
makes source retrieval available as a tool.

45
00:03:20,786 --> 00:03:22,776
We will inspect the actual reply.

46
00:03:24,600 --> 00:03:29,262
The model explains the medicine using a recorded Singapore health source, and the chat

47
00:03:29,282 --> 00:03:31,672
labels the answer as coming from the assistant.

48
00:03:32,102 --> 00:03:35,572
The trace page will show the underlying tool calls and their results.

49
00:03:37,200 --> 00:03:42,660
Now I ask whether to double a dose. The deterministic safety boundary refuses to make

50
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:47,410
that medication decision. It offers a way to raise the question with a doctor instead.

51
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:54,309
The words I have chest pain trigger the safety rules before any model request.

52
00:03:54,759 --> 00:03:59,049
The red answer points to the Singapore emergency ambulance number, nine nine five.

53
00:03:59,479 --> 00:04:01,149
The app has not called anyone.

54
00:04:03,167 --> 00:04:08,134
The dedicated help page repeats the verified contact route and states what the app has

55
00:04:08,154 --> 00:04:13,904
not done. This is guidance to seek help, not a diagnosis or a monitoring service.

56
00:04:15,067 --> 00:04:19,719
The trace page reports the current configuration: whether live model calls are

57
00:04:19,739 --> 00:04:23,929
attempted, which model is named, and a fingerprint for the prompts.

58
00:04:24,199 --> 00:04:26,429
It never displays an API key.

59
00:04:28,133 --> 00:04:31,785
Safety and boundary rules run before the language model.

60
00:04:32,115 --> 00:04:36,665
The rule set shows twenty one enabled rules and two held for review.

61
00:04:36,955 --> 00:04:40,565
That is a limited, inspectable set, not clinical validation.

62
00:04:41,767 --> 00:04:47,063
The session log records routing decisions and tool call outcomes, including an

63
00:04:47,083 --> 00:04:52,643
unsuccessful call if one occurred. It is evidence of system actions, not a view into

64
00:04:52,663 --> 00:04:53,993
private model reasoning.

65
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:59,101
Here is the same app deliberately running without model access.

66
00:04:59,751 --> 00:05:05,891
The visible banner says limited mode. Recording, trends, visit preparation and the

67
00:05:05,911 --> 00:05:08,281
fixed emergency path remain available.

68
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:12,266
The fallback answers through a small deterministic router.

69
00:05:12,756 --> 00:05:16,546
Where it cannot explain a free text question, it says so.

70
00:05:17,076 --> 00:05:20,346
The safety gate still works even with no language model.

71
00:05:21,767 --> 00:05:26,292
Back in the live instance, the appointment page assembles a fourteen day summary from

72
00:05:26,312 --> 00:05:30,982
stored facts. Nothing here books a visit, contacts a clinic, or sends a document.

73
00:05:33,800 --> 00:05:38,976
The summary includes coverage and blood pressure counts with the period they describe.

74
00:05:39,546 --> 00:05:42,896
A corrected entry is tracked without double counting.

75
00:05:43,706 --> 00:05:47,776
Missing days remain visible rather than becoming an invented zero.

76
00:05:48,333 --> 00:05:53,591
The medication section distinguishes four states, including no record at all.

77
00:05:53,901 --> 00:05:57,011
That last state cannot be called a missed dose.

78
00:05:57,561 --> 00:06:01,151
These are descriptions of what was recorded, not treatment advice.

79
00:06:02,567 --> 00:06:06,464
The patient can bring questions and reported difficulties into the appointment.

80
00:06:06,834 --> 00:06:11,294
The summary separates their words from the app's calculated facts, keeping the

81
00:06:11,314 --> 00:06:13,084
provenance of each claim clear.

82
00:06:14,633 --> 00:06:17,735
I can leave questions out of the printed document.

83
00:06:17,985 --> 00:06:22,915
The control changes to put back in the summary, so this choice is reversible.

84
00:06:23,285 --> 00:06:25,735
It does not delete the underlying patient record.

85
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:31,436
This is the print view the user can save as a PDF or carry into the visit.

86
00:06:31,766 --> 00:06:36,716
It keeps the time window and caveats. It has never been automatically shared.

87
00:06:37,967 --> 00:06:42,000
For the build workflow, we used WorkBuddy on bounded tasks.

88
00:06:42,350 --> 00:06:46,950
The saved development conversation shows its implementation of a system statistics

89
00:06:46,970 --> 00:06:52,420
endpoint and a single instance deployment guide, alongside a sample API result.

90
00:06:54,033 --> 00:06:59,136
A practical tool tip is to give the agent a small deliverable and an observable check,

91
00:06:59,446 --> 00:07:02,176
then inspect the changed files and run tests.

92
00:07:02,646 --> 00:07:05,536
An AI tool response alone is not verification.

93
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:10,598
CareSteps remains a prototype with simulated records.

94
00:07:10,908 --> 00:07:15,428
The health content has not been clinically reviewed, the app has no hospital integration

95
00:07:15,448 --> 00:07:21,118
or real authentication, and the rules cannot guarantee detection of every emergency.
